                "senderName": "NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 7 at 5:22PM MDT until September 7 at 7:15PM MDT by NWS El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa NM",
                "description": "FFWEPZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in El Paso Tx/Santa Teresa has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEastern Grant County in southwestern New Mexico...\n\n* Until 715 PM MDT.\n\n* At 522 PM MDT, Slow moving thunderstorms near Emory Pass have\nproduced around an inch of rain upstream of several campgrounds on\nHighway 152, west of the Pass. Additional thunderstorms are\nexpected to move over the area.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, highways, as\nwell as other poor drainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHighway 152 west of Emory Pass, Iron Creek Campground, Railroad\nCampround, and Upper Gallinas Campground.",
                "instruction": "Be aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.",
